<article class="env-lemma" id="0BHR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BHR">Lemma <span data-tag="0BHR">89.6.3</span>.</a> Let $(A, \mathfrak m)$ be a local Noetherian ring. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $A$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$A$ is analytically unramified (Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/032X" data-tag="032X">10.162.9</a>), 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X$ is locally of finite type over $A$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is étale at every point of codimension $0$ in $X$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then the normalization of $X$ is finite over $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a scheme $U$ and a surjective étale morphism $U \to X$. Then $U \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ satisfies the assumptions and hence the conclusions of Resolution of Surfaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BG8" data-tag="0BG8">54.11.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>